import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';
import UserTable from './UserTable';

const UserTableContainer = () =&gt; {
  const [users, setUsers] = useState([]);

  useEffect(() =&gt; {
    fetch('https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/users')
      .then((response) =&gt; response.json())
      .then((data) =&gt; setUsers(data));
  }, []);

  return &lt;UserTable users={users} /&gt;;
};

export default UserTableContainer;
```

In this code, we use the ```useState``` and ```useEffect``` hooks to manage the state of the ```users``` array. In the ```useEffect``` hook, we fetch the user data from the API using the ```fetch``` function and update the state of the ```users``` array with the data returned by the API.

We then pass the ```users``` array as a prop to the presentational component, ```UserTable```.

Here's the code for the presentational component (```UserTable.js```):javascript
