        ))}
      &lt;/tbody&gt;
    &lt;/table&gt;
  );
};

export default UserTable;
```

In this code, we receive the ```users``` prop passed down from the container component and use it to render a table with the user data. We use the ```map``` function to iterate over the ```users``` array and generate a row for each user.

Finally, we export the ```UserTable``` component so that it can be used by the container component.

To use these components in your app, you can simply import the ```UserTableContainer``` component and render it in your app:javascript
```javascript
import React from 'react';
import UserTableContainer from './UserTableContainer';

const App = () =&gt; {
  return (
    &lt;div&gt;
      &lt;h1&gt;User List&lt;/h1&gt;
      &lt;UserTableContainer /&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
  );
};

export default App;
```

This will render a table with the list of users fetched from the API by the container component.

